        "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>Plate 5 — St. James Hall, Ira E. Davenport Farewell Tour Poster (1879)</title>\n<script>\nwindow.MathJax = {\n  tex: { inlineMath: [['$', '$']], displayMath: [['$$', '$$']] }\n};\n</script>\n<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js\" async></script>\n<style>\n  html, body {\n    background: #ffffff;\n    margin: 0;\n    padding: 0;\n  }\n  body {\n    font-family: \"Times New Roman\", Times, serif;\n    color: #111;\n  }\n  .sheet {\n    width: 960px;\n    max-width: 100%;\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    padding: 24px 30px 30px 30px;\n    box-sizing: border-box;\n  }\n  .center { text-align: center; }\n  .plate {\n    text-align: center;\n    font-size: 26px;\n    letter-spacing: 2px;\n    margin: 6px 0 12px 0;\n  }\n  .hall {\n    text-align: center;\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    font-weight: 900;\n    font-size: 74px;\n    line-height: 0.95;\n    letter-spacing: 2px;\n    margin: 0;\n  }\n  .sunday {\n    text-align: center;\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    font-size: 40px;\n    line-height: 1.05;\n    letter-spacing: 0px;\n    margin: 8px 0 10px 0;\n  }\n  .rule-double {\n    border: 0;\n    border-top: 3px solid #111;\n    border-bottom: 1px solid #111;\n    height: 4px;\n    margin: 10px 0 8px 0;\n  }\n  .farewell {\n    text-align: center;\n    font-size: 40px;\n    letter-spacing: 8px;\n    margin: 6px 0 4px 0;\n  }\n  .after-six {\n    text-align: center;\n    font-size: 19px;\n    letter-spacing: 1px;\n    margin: 0 0 4px 0;\n  }\n  .ira {\n    text-align: center;\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    font-weight: 900;\n    font-size: 58px;\n    letter-spacing: 1px;\n    margin: 2px 0 2px 0;\n  }\n  .survivor {\n    text-align: center;\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    font-size: 25px;\n    margin: 2px 0 4px 0;\n  }\n  .brothers {\n    text-align: center;\n    font-family: \"Arial Narrow\", Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    font-weight: 900;\n    font-size: 78px;\n    line-height: 0.95;\n    letter-spacing: -1px;\n    margin: 2px 0 4px 0;\n  }\n  .and-small {\n    text-align: center;\n    font-size: 18px;\n    letter-spacing: 3px;\n    margin: 2px 0 2px 0;\n  }\n  .and-small span {\n    border-left: 2px solid #111;\n    border-right: 2px solid #111;\n    padding: 0 6px;\n  }\n  .prof-day {\n    text-align: center;\n    font-family: Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", serif;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    font-size: 68px;\n    letter-spacing: 4px;\n    margin: 2px 0 6px 0;\n  }\n  .previous {\n    text-align: center;\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    font-size: 26px;\n    margin: 4px 0 14px 0;\n  }\n  .placeholder {\n    width: 760px;\n    height: 470px;\n    margin: 10px auto 14px auto;\n    border: 1px solid #111;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    text-align: center;\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    font-size: 15px;\n    color: #333;\n    background: #f4f4f4;\n    box-sizing: border-box;\n    padding: 10px;\n  }\n  .unique {\n    text-align: center;\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    font-size: 30px;\n    letter-spacing: 2px;\n    margin: 8px 0 6px 0;\n  }\n  p.body {\n    font-size: 14.5px;\n    line-height: 1.28;\n    text-align: justify;\n    margin: 4px 0;\n  }\n  p.body.indent { text-indent: 26px; }\n  .powers {\n    text-align: center;\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    font-weight: 900;\n    font-size: 40px;\n    letter-spacing: 3px;\n    margin: 8px 0 6px 0;\n  }\n  .powers .orn {\n    font-size: 20px;\n    letter-spacing: 0;\n    vertical-align: middle;\n  }\n  .challenge {\n    text-align: center;\n    font-family: Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", serif;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    font-size: 46px;\n    letter-spacing: 2px;\n    margin: 12px 0 8px 0;\n  }\n  .light {\n    text-align: center;\n    font-family: Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", serif;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    font-size: 34px;\n    letter-spacing: 3px;\n    margin: 8px 0 8px 0;\n  }\n  .sc { font-variant: small-caps; }\n  .italic { font-style: italic; }\n  .boldital { font-style: italic; font-weight: 700; }\n  .footer-rule {\n    border: 0;\n    border-top: 2px solid #111;\n    margin: 26px 0 12px 0;\n  }\n  .footer {\n    text-align: center;\n    font-variant: small-caps;\n    font-size: 22px;\n    line-height: 1.45;\n    letter-spacing: 0.5px;\n    margin: 6px 0 0 0;\n  }\n  .footer .just { text-align: justify; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"sheet\">\n\n  <div class=\"plate\">PLATE 5.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"hall\">ST. JAMES HALL,</div>\n  <div class=\"sunday\">ON SUNDAY EVENING, FEBRUARY 23d, 1879.</div>\n\n  <hr class=\"rule-double\">\n\n  <div class=\"farewell\">FAREWELL TOUR!</div>\n  <div class=\"after-six\">AFTER SIX YEARS ABSENCE IN FOREIGN COUNTRIES,</div>\n\n  <div class=\"ira\">IRA E. DAVENPORT</div>\n  <div class=\"survivor\">Survivor of the World Renowned</div>\n\n  <div class=\"brothers\">DAVENPORT BROTHERS</div>\n\n  <div class=\"and-small\"><span>A N D</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"prof-day\">PROF. J. F. DAY</div>\n\n  <div class=\"previous\">Previous to their departure to Mexico and South America.</div>\n\n  <figure class=\"placeholder\">\n    [Engraving: centered — seance scene with seated and standing men, ropes, table, floating figures, tambourine, guitar and violin on floor]\n  </figure>\n\n  <div class=\"unique\">In Unique and Startling Wonders!</div>\n\n  <p class=\"body center\" style=\"text-align:center;\">Mysterious displays, and unaccountable Mysteries, which have been given in the presence of the Crowned Heads and Nobility of, Europe,<br>\n  and before large and intelligent assemblages throughout the civilized World. &nbsp; Their profoundly</p>\n\n  <div class=\"powers\"><span class=\"orn\">[ornament]</span> MYSTERIOUS &nbsp; POWERS <span class=\"orn\">[ornament]</span></div>\n\n  <p class=\"body\">Have astonished the wisest of all countries, and the most learned have been forced by overwhelming evidence to acknowledge them as inexplicable. &nbsp; <span class=\"boldital\">No complicated or glittering apparatus for deception used.</span></p>\n\n  <p class=\"body indent\">Notwithstanding the absurd and extravagant pretentions of various mountebanks and imitators, the Davenport Wonders still remain as profound a Mystery as ever.</p>\n\n  <div class=\"challenge\">CHALLENGE?</div>\n\n  <p class=\"body indent\">These gentlemen challenge all Exposers including <span class=\"sc\">Baldwin</span>, <span class=\"sc\">Bishop</span> and <span class=\"sc\">Kellog</span>, also Prof. <span class=\"sc\">Keller</span>: none of whom dare meet them &nbsp; The following Startling Wonders and Mysterious Movements are all produced in the</p>\n\n  <div class=\"light\">LIGHT,</div>\n\n  <p class=\"body\"><span class=\"italic\">and positively in full view of the entire audience.</span> &nbsp; Musical Instruments are made to play in the most extraordinary manner, and in the most profound and mysterious way. &nbsp; Human hands and arms become visible, and many other interesting experiments are presented, originating only with the Davenport Brothers in the year 1855, and never produced with success by imitators. &nbsp; Every opportunity will be given for the closest inspection by the public and press of this city &nbsp; Skeptics are especially invited to be present and occupy front seats. &nbsp; Come and see for yourselves; take no one's word. &nbsp; Examine and believe your own eyes, be guided by your own reason, as all of the above, through ignorance and superstition, has been attributed to WITCHCRAFT and DEMONOLOGY.</p>\n\n  <hr class=\"footer-rule\">\n\n  <div class=\"footer\">\n    Portion of Poster Advertising Ira E. Davenport's Entertainment after<br>\n    the Death of His Brother, W. H. Davenport. \" Prof. J. F. Day \" was<br>\n    a Conjurer who Already was Performing the Davenport Tricks when<br>\n    W. H. Davenport Died. &nbsp; U.S.A. 1879.\n  </div>\n\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>"
